{"message": "GUI speech request: To make an orb vibrate instead of rotating, you can use CSS animations. Here's a simple example of how you can achieve that:\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <style>\n        .orb {\n            width: 100px;\n            height: 100px;\n            background-color: blue;\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            position: relative;\n            animation: vibrate 0.1s infinite;\n        }\n\n        @keyframes vibrate {\n            0% { transform: translate(0px, 0px); }\n            25% { transform: translate(2px, 0px); }\n            50% { transform: translate(0px, 2px); }\n            75% { transform: translate(-2px, 0px); }\n            100% { transform: translate(0px, -2px); }\n        }\n    </style>\n    <title>Vibrating Orb</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div class=\"orb\"></div>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\nIn this code, a CSS animation is defined to make an orb element vibrate by shifting its position slightly back and forth. You can adjust the `translate` values and `animation` duration to change the intensity and speed of the vibration.", "level": "INFO", "name": "avi-livekit", "timestamp": "2026-10-09T13:16:06.948873+00:00"}
